## Reproduction and provenance
- `code/fit.py` generates the data (seed 217), runs the fit and writes `results/fit.json` and `results/data.csv`. Run from the repository root with `python code/fit.py` (needs numpy and scipy).
- `figures/make_fit_figure.py` draws the figure from `figures/data.csv` and `figures/fit.json` (copies of `results/data.csv` and `results/fit.json`); run it from `figures/`.
- Every number in this report comes from `results/fit.json`; none was computed in the report.

## Caveats
This is a single simulated realisation. That both CIs cover the truth is consistent with the nominal 95% level but does not test coverage. The reading of "drawn using `default_rng(217)`" as one `normal(0, 3, 40)` call is an assumption.
